+++ b/docs/plans/2026-10-19-derived-pure-result-persistence-profile.md
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+Status: implemented; contract lives in `specs/state.md` ("Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile").
+
+## Approach
+
+Eligible (acyclic, single-visit) compiler-generated `pure_projection` successes persist only a
+value-free completion shell; resume re-derives the values in memory from durable inputs.
+
+- `orchestrator/state.py`: `RunState.result_persistence_profile`, `StateManager.initialize(...)`
+  keyword, fail-closed validation, atomic `begin_/reuse_/settle_eligible_pure_*` visit methods.
+- `orchestrator/workflow/pure_replay_errors.py`, `pure_replay_progress.py` (shell, witness,
+  classification), `pure_replay_index.py` (eligibility + dependency index),
+  `pure_replay_runtime.py` (overlay replay, audits); `pure_result_replay.py` is the import facade.
+- Executor: visit/cursor and settlement for eligible nodes, no result bundle or lineage for them,
+  resume audits (surfaces, progress), overlay replay after the default-resume decision, restart
+  boundary determined once, provider observation manager created at execution start.
+- Checkpoints: eligible pure points emit no record, their bindings are not captured, and they are
+  filtered from the unique-nearest durable boundary; the one zero-record default-resume case is
+  `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`.
+- Selection: `run` of a compiled `.orc`, `resume --force-restart` roots, and fresh Workflow Lisp
+  callee frames (from callee provenance).
+
+## Makes harder
+
+- Pure values are no longer inspectable in `state.json`; debugging uses the replayed overlay.
+- Resume re-evaluates pure nodes, so evaluator changes alter replayed values (guarded by payload
+  digests only through the existing pure-expression validation).
+- Eligibility is conservative: nodes that publish/consume artifact lineage, or depend on
+  ineligible pure nodes, keep historical persistence.
+
+## Verification
+
+`tests/test_pure_result_replay_{state,index,runtime,resume,default_resume,frames,cli}.py`.
