   Root/callee checksums, lexical checkpoint validation, and
   projection-integrity guards remain unchanged.
 
+## Derived Pure-Result Persistence Profile
+
+`result_persistence_profile: "derived_pure_replay.v1"` stores each *eligible*
+compiler-generated `pure_projection` success as a value-free completion shell
+and rebuilds the values at resume from durable inputs, in memory.
+
+- Selection
+  - `StateManager.initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=...)` writes the field atomically when the state is created, before any visit. Loads never infer, backfill, or upgrade it; generic `initialize` callers stay explicit opt-in.
+  - `orchestrator run` of a successfully compiled typed `.orc` workflow, and the new root created by `orchestrator resume --force-restart`, select the profile. Force restart leaves the source run byte-for-byte unchanged and the new root keeps the requested observability settings.
+  - A fresh non-iterative child call frame selects it exactly when the callee bundle's validated provenance has `frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"`, never from the parent's profile, a path suffix, an alias, or a step identity. A fresh retry after a failed non-iterative Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state and selects it; the failed predecessor is unchanged. Existing roots/frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees, and iteration-owned child frames keep the historical profile, and an existing frame is never backfilled. An existing frame without a mapping `state` is rejected with `ValueError("... existing call-frame state ...")` before anything is written.
+- Eligibility (`orchestrator.workflow.pure_result_replay.derive_pure_result_replay_index`)
+  - Eligible: compiler-generated `pure_projection` nodes that are acyclic and visited at most once per scope. Recurrent, loop-owned, other multiply visited pure nodes, nodes that publish or consume artifact lineage, and nodes depending on such pure nodes keep full durable rows, bundles, and checkpoints (`ineligible_pure_reasons[node_id]`, e.g. `multiple_visit_region`).
+  - Refs are scoped to the workflow that holds them; an imported callee bundle indexes only its own nodes under its own `"root"` scope. Only exact `{"ref": ...}` leaves form dependency edges; every literal subtree (including inactive union members) must match its declared binding type.
+  - Index failures raise `PureResultReplayIndexError` (`code == "pure_result_replay_unavailable"`) with `reason` one of `dependency_index_invalid`, `reachability_ambiguous`, `multiple_visit_region`, `progress_witness_invalid`, `profile_conflict`. The index is derived without mutating or serializing the program.
+- Durable shape
+  - Success: exactly `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0, "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed", "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}`; any extra or wrong key (`value`, `output`, `artifacts`, `debug`, `duration_ms`, ...) is invalid. Failed and skipped rows stay full durable rows. No pure result bundle, no `private_artifact_versions` entry, and no checkpoint record or restore binding exists for an eligible node.
+  - Each visit is atomic: `begin_eligible_pure_visit` publishes the visit and its running cursor together; `settle_eligible_pure_success` / `settle_eligible_pure_failure` write the row and clear the cursor together.
+  - Progress classes (`classify_pure_replay_progress`): `unstarted`, `interrupted` (visit + matching cursor), `derived_complete` (visit + exact shell), `durable_failure_skip`; anything else (visit-two cursor or shell, cursor plus row, mismatched identity, value-bearing completion, ...) is `progress_witness_invalid`.
+- Resume
+  - Before the prologue a resumed run audits persisted surfaces (a value row, pure bundle, private-lineage entry, checkpoint record, or restore binding for an eligible node raises `profile_conflict` with `context["surface"]` in `steps`, `pure_bundle`, `private_artifact_versions`, `checkpoint_record`, `restore_payload` before any write) and progress witnesses.
+  - Needed pure values are re-derived in an in-memory overlay from durable inputs; replay never dispatches an effect, increments a visit, settles a result, or writes durable state. Unrecoverable replay fails the run closed before any effect with `error.type == "pure_result_replay_unavailable"` and `error.context.reason` one of `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`, `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`.
+  - The restart boundary is determined once per resume. With no durable checkpoint owner before the restart node, default resume admits one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY` (`selection_reason: validated_frame_entry_replay`, `checkpoint_id: null`), only when the profile, progress witnesses, and bound-input leaves validate; otherwise it fails closed with `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`. Replay-eligible pure points are filtered out of the durable checkpoint candidates before unique-nearest selection, so selection never scans past an invalid nearest durable boundary.
+
 ## Reusable-Call State Contract (v2.5)
 
 - Caller-visible exports
